<title>INDIA: Indian bank staff to strike work on Feb 28 - union.</title>
<headline>Indian bank staff to strike work on Feb 28 - union.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank employees all over India have threatened to go on strike on February 28 unless a Calcutta based state-run bank revokes its decision to freeze the wages of its employees, a bank union said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The federal government presents its budget for 1997/98 (April-March) on February 28.</p>
<p>The All-India Central Bank Officers' Association said all the bank unions, representing India's entire bank staff, had joined together to protest against the decision of the UCO Bank to freeze its employees' wages.</p>
<p>UCO Bank is a loss-making bank and reported a net loss of 2.37 billion rupees for 1995/96 (April-March).</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
